1
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:30,920
Owada City, lightly surpassing the times

2
00:00:32,820 --> 00:00:37,440
diving into the city,
playing at being a hero

3
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:39,340
I wanna spend time with you forever

4
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:45,100
so we keep wearing nothing
but the latest trends

5
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:49,220
because a natural face is
what sells out instantly

6
00:00:50,040 --> 00:00:51,000
Let it ring!

7
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:55,040
Everybody can do, we've started running

8
00:00:55,040 --> 00:00:58,220
Dreams never stop

9
00:00:58,220 --> 00:01:02,460
Let's set sail again tomorrow

10
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:03,500
Let me run

11
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:06,140
Everybody can do

12
00:01:06,140 --> 00:01:10,820
Even if we stick out a little,
it doesn't hurt

13
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:15,000
holding onto our noisy curiosity

14
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:17,860
Stay strong, stay high, stay up

15
00:01:29,360 --> 00:01:31,400
New Year Battle Karuta

16
00:01:46,860 --> 00:01:48,220
Alright, it's done.

17
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:50,980
Thanks for working through New Year's.

18
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:53,900
We'll take over from here.

19
00:01:55,180 --> 00:01:56,180
Good work.

20
00:01:56,180 --> 00:01:59,760
Ryo-san, you've been on duty since New Year's Eve,
haven't you?

21
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:01,280
Of course.

22
00:02:01,660 --> 00:02:03,140
Unlike Nakagawa and Reiko,

23
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:06,340
I'm devoted to my duty at this police box,
you know.

24
00:02:06,740 --> 00:02:11,480
I'm fired up with the passionate mission of protecting the common people,
even over New Year's.

25
00:02:12,320 --> 00:02:13,500
What's so funny?

26
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:17,000
Dad, your jokes are as
bushy as your eyebrows.

27
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:17,720
What?

28
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:21,060
We know.
You took too many summer days off last year.

29
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:24,180
So now you're making up for
it over New Year's, right?

30
00:02:25,040 --> 00:02:26,540
So you knew, did you?

31
00:02:29,180 --> 00:02:30,980
Well, guess I'll head home now.

32
00:02:30,980 --> 00:02:32,820
Ryo-san, what are you gonna do now?

33
00:02:32,820 --> 00:02:35,300
I'm just gonna knock back
some cold sake and go to sleep.

34
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:38,460
There's no New Year's party at the Chief's house this year,
after all.

35
00:02:38,460 --> 00:02:39,740
That's weird.

36
00:02:39,740 --> 00:02:43,040
I ran into Terai at the first
shrine visit yesterday, but

37
00:02:43,480 --> 00:02:47,660
he said he was going to make New
Year's visits to the Chief's house.

38
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:49,860
That must be some kind of mistake.

39
00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:54,240
The Chief said he's going on a family trip,
just the family together.

40
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:57,960
New Year's party?

41
00:02:58,400 --> 00:03:01,180
It's the annual New Year's party held at the Chief's house,
you know.

42
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:03,160
When's it going to be next year?

43
00:03:05,380 --> 00:03:07,080
Next year it's canceled.

44
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:17,300
Eating osechi at the Chief's house
was my biggest New Year's treat!

45
00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:19,500
Ryo-chan, you're being so dramatic.

46
00:03:21,560 --> 00:03:23,280
Well, don't be so disappointed.

47
00:03:25,040 --> 00:03:27,160
The three of us are
going on a hot spring trip.

48
00:03:27,660 --> 00:03:30,200
So you value your family
over your subordinates?

49
00:03:30,920 --> 00:03:33,680
Don't say that. Hiromi's at that age too.

50
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:37,780
We can't take a trip just the two
of us like this many more times.

51
00:03:38,740 --> 00:03:40,020
Well, that's how it is.

52
00:03:40,540 --> 00:03:43,600
Everyone, the New Year's party
will be the year after next.

53
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:44,600
Y-yes.

54
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:47,040
R-really, what a shame.

55
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:52,620
Looking back,
everyone was acting incredibly unnatural.

56
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:55,660
Could it be that I'm the
only one who wasn't invited?

57
00:03:56,380 --> 00:03:56,780
Right.

58
00:03:59,660 --> 00:04:04,780
Is this Terai's residence?

59
00:04:04,780 --> 00:04:06,000
This is Ryotsu.

60
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,380
Happy New Year.

61
00:04:08,100 --> 00:04:11,540
By the way,
I actually have some business with Terai.

62
00:04:14,260 --> 00:04:14,720
Hm?

63
00:04:15,220 --> 00:04:16,100
What?!

64
00:04:19,740 --> 00:04:21,180
Y-you got me good.

65
00:04:34,840 --> 00:04:36,080
I won't forgive you!

66
00:04:37,740 --> 00:04:40,400
Ryo-san,
you didn't have a chance just now, did you?

67
00:04:40,860 --> 00:04:42,300
Well, this is going to get bloody.

68
00:04:45,540 --> 00:04:47,760
Happy New Year.

69
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:51,040
You came. Looking forward to
working with you again this year.

70
00:04:52,380 --> 00:04:54,280
Hiromi-chan, you look cute.

71
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:57,580
You look great too, Reiko-san. Thank you.

72
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:01,080
Hasn't the senior officer arrived yet?

73
00:05:06,020 --> 00:05:07,460
Honestly, Daddy...

74
00:05:07,460 --> 00:05:12,220
Hiromi, I don't even want to
think about that guy on New Year's.

75
00:05:12,660 --> 00:05:15,740
Anyway, did Nakagawa park
his car in front of the house?

76
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:21,100
Come on, come in.
It's a bit cramped, but come in.

77
00:05:22,380 --> 00:05:26,460
Chief, why are you closing
the windows in broad daylight?

78
00:05:27,140 --> 00:05:29,620
I guess it's some kind of
charm to ward off demons.

79
00:05:30,220 --> 00:05:31,400
Warding off demons.

80
00:05:34,220 --> 00:05:37,038
Ow But senpai, please have mercy!

81
00:05:37,088 --> 00:05:40,100
I'm just about to go to the shrine
for New Year's with my sister.

82
00:05:40,260 --> 00:05:42,528
You can visit a shrine for
New Year's anytime, though.

83
00:05:42,578 --> 00:05:44,760
But the Chief's New
Year's party is only today!

84
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:46,820
That's ridiculous.

85
00:05:47,220 --> 00:05:48,413
Doesn't it make you mad?

86
00:05:48,463 --> 00:05:51,260
You weren't invited to the New Year's party either,
you know.

87
00:05:51,940 --> 00:05:53,812
Of course. I'm on temporary duty,

88
00:05:53,862 --> 00:05:56,080
and I'm not stationed at the police box.

89
00:05:56,320 --> 00:05:59,190
Stop nitpicking. We're best friends, so

90
00:05:59,240 --> 00:06:01,460
just take me to the Chief's house.

91
00:06:01,460 --> 00:06:04,460
Aaaaaah!

92
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:13,520
Aaaaaah!

93
00:06:13,520 --> 00:06:15,140
Eeeeeeh?

94
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:23,640
Pushy old geezer,
starting the New Year like this.

95
00:06:24,340 --> 00:06:26,720
Fine, fine. Just hop on already.

96
00:06:42,220 --> 00:06:43,440
Sorry.

97
00:06:45,300 --> 00:06:46,340
What is it, Nakagawa?

98
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:48,920
That engine sound just now...

99
00:06:48,920 --> 00:06:51,180
Isn't that Honda-san's CBX?

100
00:06:51,940 --> 00:06:53,920
Could it be that the
senior officer came too?

101
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:57,260
He's already caught wind of it?

102
00:06:57,740 --> 00:07:00,140
Even a devil's nose sniffs things out well.

103
00:07:00,960 --> 00:07:01,540
Listen up.

104
00:07:16,760 --> 00:07:17,100
Yeah?

105
00:07:17,420 --> 00:07:19,000
Yeah, he's playing dead,
pretending he's not home.

106
00:07:19,980 --> 00:07:22,900
Didn't he really go on
that family trip after all?

107
00:07:23,390 --> 00:07:25,660
That can't be! Look at that!

108
00:07:27,460 --> 00:07:28,440
What's that?

109
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:32,320
Tailing us like that, what a cheap trick!

110
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:38,460
It's a Ferrari F50.

111
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:47,820
It's not the one he always drives, but it's definitely Nakagawa's Ferrari.
Are you sure? Couldn't it belong to a neighbor?

112
00:07:47,820 --> 00:07:53,720
Look around properly. Where on earth does anyone live here?
Let me check the license plate.

113
00:07:55,780 --> 00:08:03,660
It's a Shonan plate. Nakagawa lives in Tokyo,
but he shows off and has all his cars registered in Shonan.

114
00:08:06,920 --> 00:08:08,480
Shh.

115
00:08:08,960 --> 00:08:10,000
Chief?

116
00:08:11,180 --> 00:08:14,080
This is a search. Please issue the warrant.

117
00:08:14,980 --> 00:08:17,060
Chief, please come out.

118
00:08:18,100 --> 00:08:19,640
Yō-chan's totally busted, isn't she?

119
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:22,660
I just feel so awkward.

120
00:08:26,260 --> 00:08:29,060
Damn it, they're really going
to keep up the act of being out.

121
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:32,940
All the houses have their
shutters and curtains closed.

122
00:08:33,260 --> 00:08:35,440
They really must have gone on a trip.

123
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:37,980
Well, the enemy is still inside after all.

124
00:08:39,080 --> 00:08:39,960
Look at this.

125
00:08:40,940 --> 00:08:43,560
This is just an electric meter, isn't it?

126
00:08:43,560 --> 00:08:45,520
Look at the meter closely.

127
00:08:46,460 --> 00:08:49,740
If they're really away, only the
fridge and the phone should be running.

128
00:08:50,160 --> 00:08:52,180
The meter wouldn't be spinning this fast.

129
00:08:52,660 --> 00:08:53,060
I see.

130
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:56,940
Everyone, is sukiyaki all right with you?

131
00:08:56,940 --> 00:09:00,140
Sounds great. We were getting
tired of the New Year's dishes.

132
00:09:00,140 --> 00:09:01,540
I'll help.

133
00:09:02,120 --> 00:09:09,740
We know you're in there, you sly things!
Open up and let us in at once!

134
00:09:11,240 --> 00:09:19,640
Be nice and let him in.
No way. You may not know it, but that man wrecked the house for the New Year's party!

135
00:09:20,440 --> 00:09:28,820
If he plays battledore, he ruins my precious bonsai.
If he does calligraphy, he stains the tatami, and when I scold him, he smears ink on my face.

136
00:09:29,540 --> 00:09:33,120
And in the end, he blackened the whole room.

137
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:36,200
I'm never letting that
man into this house again.

138
00:09:36,720 --> 00:09:40,500
I can't really blame you
for leaving our senior out.

139
00:09:41,040 --> 00:09:43,820
You're completely surrounded.

140
00:09:43,820 --> 00:09:45,800
Give up and come out.

141
00:09:45,800 --> 00:09:47,000
Ignore them, ignore them.

142
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:49,760
There's no reaction at all

143
00:09:50,200 --> 00:09:52,740
Damn it, if that's how you want it,

144
00:09:52,740 --> 00:09:55,300
let's go with our trump
card and force our way in.

145
00:09:55,760 --> 00:09:56,520
Trump card?

146
00:09:58,200 --> 00:09:59,660
It's gone quiet, hasn't it.

147
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:02,820
Looks like they've given up.

148
00:10:02,820 --> 00:10:07,760
No, when food is involved,
Senpai shows an incredible determination.

149
00:10:07,760 --> 00:10:09,300
I wouldn't relax yet.

150
00:10:10,320 --> 00:10:11,460
Is it a power outage?

151
00:10:12,140 --> 00:10:14,840
No way they'd do electrical
work on New Year's.

152
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:18,860
Dear, the gas in the
kitchen suddenly stopped too.

153
00:10:18,860 --> 00:10:19,780
What?

154
00:10:20,900 --> 00:10:23,860
This is all Ryotsu's doing!

155
00:10:24,440 --> 00:10:28,180
Senpai, let's just stop here already.

156
00:10:28,180 --> 00:10:32,360
Shut up! Now I'm going to
eat that osechi no matter what!

157
00:10:33,860 --> 00:10:35,440
Still, they're stubborn, aren't they.

158
00:10:36,060 --> 00:10:40,640
Flooding them out by reversing the water and
sewer lines would be fun for people like this,

159
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:43,600
but let's just smash the door down faster.

160
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:45,220
Wait, wait, wait, senpai!

161
00:10:50,300 --> 00:10:53,200
Senpai, you're serious? A chainsaw?

162
00:10:53,860 --> 00:10:56,080
Relax, it's fine. Don't worry.

163
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:59,720
For now, we'll only break the minimum.

164
00:10:59,920 --> 00:11:01,940
I can't relax at all!

165
00:11:02,400 --> 00:11:03,560
Here goes! Let's move!

166
00:11:05,820 --> 00:11:07,480
Kwaaah! Ryotsu!

167
00:11:18,560 --> 00:11:22,960
Chief! Don't open the door so suddenly!
You nearly shortened my life!

168
00:11:23,860 --> 00:11:25,820
It was me whose life nearly got shortened.

169
00:11:26,400 --> 00:11:30,100
Senpai,
what are you doing here with a chainsaw?

170
00:11:30,100 --> 00:11:30,900
The door...

171
00:11:30,900 --> 00:11:35,460
The Chief asked me to trim his plants.

172
00:11:36,440 --> 00:11:39,820
Liar! I don't remember
asking you to do that.

173
00:11:39,820 --> 00:11:42,860
Ugh, getting older makes you so forgetful.

174
00:11:43,580 --> 00:11:44,480
Hey, Honda.

175
00:11:44,900 --> 00:11:45,260
Yes?

176
00:11:47,340 --> 00:11:51,300
Anyway, Chief,
didn't you go on a hot spring trip?

177
00:11:52,580 --> 00:11:56,380
That was a mix-up at the travel agency.

178
00:11:56,380 --> 00:11:59,240
I couldn't get tickets,
so I ended up staying home.

179
00:11:59,980 --> 00:12:02,340
Then why is Nakagawa here?

180
00:12:04,460 --> 00:12:06,480
So I suddenly had some free time,

181
00:12:06,480 --> 00:12:08,860
so I invited Nakagawa and Reiko.

182
00:12:09,460 --> 00:12:13,080
Of course, I did contact you
properly at the Nikoniko dormitory,

183
00:12:13,080 --> 00:12:14,560
but unfortunately you were out.

184
00:12:14,560 --> 00:12:16,160
Well, of course I was out!

185
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:18,940
I've been stationed at Ashisuke all this time,
you know.

186
00:12:19,740 --> 00:12:20,760
Was that so?

187
00:12:21,300 --> 00:12:23,220
Haha, I completely forgot.

188
00:12:25,160 --> 00:12:28,960
Well, running into each other like this must be fate.
Why don't you stop by for a bit, Honda?

189
00:12:30,560 --> 00:12:32,780
Chief, that's fine, of course, right?

190
00:12:35,120 --> 00:12:38,460
Lucky you, Honda, coming all the
way to Chiba to trim the garden trees.

191
00:12:39,700 --> 00:12:42,160
Well then,
shall we be treated to the New Year's food?

192
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:44,220
Before that.

193
00:12:49,820 --> 00:12:50,940
Sorry to keep you waiting.

194
00:12:52,300 --> 00:12:55,120
For someone who came to the New Year's routine,
you're well prepared.

195
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:58,380
I brought these so we wouldn't be in
trouble if something like this happened.

196
00:12:58,380 --> 00:13:01,120
Honda, dressed like that,
you're being a bit rude.

197
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:03,880
Well, never mind, it's the Chief's house.

198
00:13:05,680 --> 00:13:09,260
Yone, you'd better remember this!

199
00:13:22,480 --> 00:13:25,500
Ryotsu-san, Honda-san, happy New Year!

200
00:13:26,020 --> 00:13:27,360
Well, sit down there.

201
00:13:27,360 --> 00:13:28,740
Thanks, thanks.

202
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:32,420
To everyone who was invited, happy New Year.

203
00:13:32,420 --> 00:13:34,020
Happy New Year.

204
00:13:34,780 --> 00:13:38,160
Terai, that new kimono suits you well.

205
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:40,500
H-how did you know that?

206
00:13:40,980 --> 00:13:43,920
If you're coming to a New Year's
party wearing a kimono that nice,

207
00:13:43,920 --> 00:13:47,100
you could at least have said something to me,
don't you think?

208
00:13:47,100 --> 00:13:47,780
Yeah.

209
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:52,960
Honda, I'm so lucky to have
such good colleagues, right?

210
00:13:52,960 --> 00:13:54,140
Senpai.

211
00:13:54,140 --> 00:13:58,480
Ryo-chan, stop with those backhanded digs.

212
00:13:58,480 --> 00:13:59,440
What did you say?

213
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:03,060
Come on, it's New Year's,
so let's have a good time.

214
00:14:03,760 --> 00:14:07,480
We're tired of New Year's food,
so I thought we'd have sukiyaki.

215
00:14:08,080 --> 00:14:09,480
How about you two join us?

216
00:14:10,640 --> 00:14:13,200
How can you do something so sacrilegious?

217
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:15,660
On New Year's,
you're supposed to eat osechi.

218
00:14:17,100 --> 00:14:18,600
That's common sense, Chief!

219
00:14:19,020 --> 00:14:20,140
But...

220
00:14:20,140 --> 00:14:23,140
Osechi isn't made just for show, you know.

221
00:14:23,140 --> 00:14:26,220
It's so housewives can get a
break from chores at New Year's.

222
00:14:26,220 --> 00:14:29,660
Packed with dishes that keep well, so no
housework is needed during the New Year.

223
00:14:29,660 --> 00:14:33,500
Eating them is the age-old
wisdom of the Japanese!

224
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:37,740
But it's not as if Ryo-chan has
anything to brag about, is it?

225
00:14:37,740 --> 00:14:38,480
Right!

226
00:14:39,400 --> 00:14:41,420
The same goes for what's in the osechi.

227
00:14:41,420 --> 00:14:43,320
Kobumaki will be delighted.

228
00:14:43,320 --> 00:14:45,520
Black beans are hard-working little beans.

229
00:14:45,520 --> 00:14:49,180
Shrimp are lucky food, and there's a
real meaning behind each dish, you know.

230
00:14:49,180 --> 00:14:53,100
What are you thinking,
having sukiyaki on New Year's?

231
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:55,920
Japanese New Year is obviously about osechi!

232
00:14:56,280 --> 00:15:00,340
It looks like the osechi is already made,
so you should bring it out.

233
00:15:01,340 --> 00:15:02,700
Looks like it, yeah.

234
00:15:03,300 --> 00:15:05,400
Mom, there's still some osechi left, right?

235
00:15:05,400 --> 00:15:06,680
Bring that out.

236
00:15:07,300 --> 00:15:07,660
Yes.

237
00:15:08,860 --> 00:15:11,000
Yay, osechi is here!

238
00:15:11,460 --> 00:15:13,663
We'll have our sukiyaki here,

239
00:15:13,713 --> 00:15:16,100
so Ryotsu, you eat your osechi over there.

240
00:15:21,060 --> 00:15:24,900
Left out again Well,
at least the osechi's coming.

241
00:15:25,580 --> 00:15:26,660
Here it comes.

242
00:15:27,100 --> 00:15:28,100
Here you go.

243
00:15:28,440 --> 00:15:30,660
Thanks. What?

244
00:15:34,500 --> 00:15:38,360
I don't see the kinton
or the kazunoko anywhere.

245
00:15:38,800 --> 00:15:42,100
We already ate those.
That's all that's left.

246
00:15:42,100 --> 00:15:46,440
Black beans? Kobumaki? Kamaboko?

247
00:15:47,140 --> 00:15:50,900
So the three least popular osechi
dishes were bound to be left over.

248
00:15:54,980 --> 00:15:59,340
Osechi without a protagonist
isn't tasty at all.

249
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:02,300
That looks delicious.

250
00:16:02,960 --> 00:16:05,200
Alright, it's cooked down nicely now.

251
00:16:06,140 --> 00:16:07,160
Chief.

252
00:16:07,660 --> 00:16:08,980
Well, shall we eat?

253
00:16:08,980 --> 00:16:10,120
Let's dig in.

254
00:16:10,680 --> 00:16:11,820
Chief.

255
00:16:12,260 --> 00:16:12,620
What is it?

256
00:16:13,720 --> 00:16:16,620
If you don't mind, shall I help
with the sukiyaki over there too?

257
00:16:16,620 --> 00:16:19,860
You're the one who wanted osechi, so I
went to the trouble of serving it to you.

258
00:16:19,860 --> 00:16:23,600
Ryotsu, you don't get any sukiyaki
until you've finished your osechi.

259
00:16:24,280 --> 00:16:25,340
Fine, fine.

260
00:16:25,340 --> 00:16:27,540
I'll eat the osechi, then.
That's what you want, right?

261
00:16:28,560 --> 00:16:29,200
Of course.

262
00:16:29,720 --> 00:16:34,100
Good. I was wondering what to do
with those leftover osechi dishes.

263
00:16:34,100 --> 00:16:36,060
They're perfect for
clearing out the leftovers.

264
00:16:36,060 --> 00:16:39,360
Ryo-chan's stomach is as tough as a viper's,
after all.

265
00:16:39,360 --> 00:16:42,560
Right, right. I'll be serving up the ones that have gone a little bad,
you know.

266
00:16:44,620 --> 00:16:49,320
Besides, Ryotsu, you'd better eat
the meat before you finish your osechi.

267
00:16:49,320 --> 00:16:49,880
Yes, yes.

268
00:16:55,360 --> 00:16:57,340
Finally, we get to eat sukiyaki!

269
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:00,640
Whoa!

270
00:17:02,020 --> 00:17:04,380
There's only one slice of meat!

271
00:17:04,980 --> 00:17:05,960
Damn it!

272
00:17:07,800 --> 00:17:08,600
What?

273
00:17:09,980 --> 00:17:13,780
Too bad. I got here first.

274
00:17:14,140 --> 00:17:17,280
No, I got here first. Honda, right?

275
00:17:17,480 --> 00:17:19,340
Honda, I'll say it straight!

276
00:17:19,660 --> 00:17:22,280
No, but, at the prince's house...

277
00:17:22,280 --> 00:17:25,220
Old folks should cut back
on meat for their health!

278
00:17:25,660 --> 00:17:29,180
You're the one who ate so much osechi,
so you should hold back!

279
00:17:30,620 --> 00:17:31,860
Ahahaha!

280
00:17:32,740 --> 00:17:34,480
Grr, damn it all!

281
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:38,780
Trying to spit on the meat won't work,
you know!

282
00:17:39,180 --> 00:17:41,500
I see right through your despicable tactics!

283
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:42,720
Ugh, it stinks!

284
00:17:43,680 --> 00:17:46,020
You two aren't kids, you know.

285
00:17:47,040 --> 00:17:49,680
I know.
Whoever wins the match gets to eat it.

286
00:17:49,680 --> 00:17:51,160
A match?

287
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:54,800
How about settling it with a karuta match,
New Year's style?

288
00:17:55,340 --> 00:17:56,380
Sounds fun.

289
00:17:57,860 --> 00:17:58,780
Fine by me.

290
00:17:58,780 --> 00:18:01,120
Wasn't there a police karuta set?

291
00:18:01,120 --> 00:18:03,260
Police karuta?

292
00:18:03,660 --> 00:18:05,700
I played that with my
little sister yesterday.

293
00:18:05,700 --> 00:18:08,340
They say even a detective who
walks will bump into a case.

294
00:18:08,340 --> 00:18:11,140
Let's see...
"Be careful for a moment, and be injured for a lifetime."

295
00:18:11,140 --> 00:18:12,560
That one's good, right?

296
00:18:13,280 --> 00:18:16,420
A karuta like those traffic
safety slogans isn't any fun.

297
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:18,100
What do you say?

298
00:18:18,340 --> 00:18:20,000
Let's play with my karuta.

299
00:18:21,160 --> 00:18:22,020
You brought it?

300
00:18:22,020 --> 00:18:24,240
Yeah, I figured something
like this might come up,

301
00:18:24,240 --> 00:18:27,020
so I made it during my New Year's duty.

302
00:18:27,020 --> 00:18:29,740
You made it while on duty?!

303
00:18:29,740 --> 00:18:31,440
Are we really doing a karuta match?

304
00:18:31,440 --> 00:18:32,940
Aren't we?

305
00:18:32,940 --> 00:18:34,760
Let's do it!

306
00:18:34,760 --> 00:18:37,540
I'll win for sure,
and you won't get any meat!

307
00:18:37,540 --> 00:18:39,280
No, the one who eats the last of the meat

308
00:18:39,280 --> 00:18:39,920
will be me!

309
00:18:42,040 --> 00:18:43,080
I'm going to eat it!

310
00:18:46,260 --> 00:18:46,660
Well then,

311
00:18:46,660 --> 00:18:47,720
here we go.

312
00:18:50,260 --> 00:18:52,580
What's wrong? Hurry up and read!

313
00:18:52,580 --> 00:18:57,040
I can't read this. Nakagawa, you take over!

314
00:18:57,040 --> 00:19:00,280
Anyone, just hurry up and read!

315
00:19:00,280 --> 00:19:01,780
Understood.

316
00:19:02,960 --> 00:19:05,720
Reiko's huge tits will sag someday.

317
00:19:05,720 --> 00:19:07,120
W-what did you say?

318
00:19:07,820 --> 00:19:09,280
Well I didn't...

319
00:19:09,280 --> 00:19:09,680
Yes.

320
00:19:11,660 --> 00:19:15,180
Chief, you go first. That's fine, right?

321
00:19:18,720 --> 00:19:19,880
That's what it says, see.

322
00:19:19,880 --> 00:19:21,060
You idiot!

323
00:19:21,060 --> 00:19:23,200
Okay, next one.

324
00:19:23,820 --> 00:19:25,920
Claws? The Chief, no doubt.

325
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:27,020
Kankichi Ryotsu

326
00:19:27,020 --> 00:19:28,220
What?

327
00:19:29,440 --> 00:19:30,540
Take it!

328
00:19:31,500 --> 00:19:33,660
This card's my favorite.

329
00:19:33,660 --> 00:19:35,860
Given that the senior made it,

330
00:19:35,860 --> 00:19:37,440
this karuta is totally crazy, isn't it.

331
00:19:38,820 --> 00:19:39,960
Black-hearted.

332
00:19:39,960 --> 00:19:41,920
Chief Ohara is a skinflint.

333
00:19:41,920 --> 00:19:43,520
What did you just say?!

334
00:19:43,520 --> 00:19:43,980
Yes.

335
00:19:45,600 --> 00:19:48,240
It was right in front of you, too bad.

336
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:54,160
Terai, stuck in home loan hell.

337
00:19:55,480 --> 00:19:56,200
Still not done

338
00:19:59,920 --> 00:20:01,280
You're being naive, Chief.

339
00:20:01,680 --> 00:20:05,100
Looks like you're no match for me,
the karuta-taking master.

340
00:20:07,240 --> 00:20:08,860
This karuta is rigged!

341
00:20:08,860 --> 00:20:12,300
You made it yourself,
so you're obviously at an advantage.

342
00:20:12,300 --> 00:20:15,040
Just because you're losing,
you're going to start picking fights?

343
00:20:15,880 --> 00:20:16,600
That's not it.

344
00:20:16,600 --> 00:20:21,740
No! The handwriting is so sloppy it's hard to read.
It's unfair if only you can make them out.

345
00:20:24,140 --> 00:20:27,520
Chief, are you going for them because
you think they're picture cards?

346
00:20:28,980 --> 00:20:31,660
I'm being fair.
I've scattered them all around.

347
00:20:34,720 --> 00:20:38,900
You plan to scatter them all over the house?
That's fair, right?

348
00:20:44,180 --> 00:20:45,200
Alright, this'll do.

349
00:20:45,620 --> 00:20:48,460
Nakagawa reads them out here,
and we search for the cards.

350
00:20:48,900 --> 00:20:51,980
When we find one,
we bring it over for Nakagawa to confirm.

351
00:20:51,980 --> 00:20:53,240
Sounds like fun.

352
00:20:54,020 --> 00:20:55,180
Alright, let's begin!

353
00:20:55,180 --> 00:20:56,300
Right.

354
00:20:57,360 --> 00:21:00,420
Nakagawa-kun,
the cop who does this as a hobby.

355
00:21:00,420 --> 00:21:01,020
Nada-na.

356
00:21:04,900 --> 00:21:06,640
Alright, found one!

357
00:21:07,160 --> 00:21:07,980
Damn it!

358
00:21:09,160 --> 00:21:12,380
Ryotsu Kankichi,
Kameari's most handsome man.

359
00:21:12,380 --> 00:21:16,580
Honda-kun,
who's been dumped more often than Tora-san.

360
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:21,320
Yes, Ryo-san! Pachinko jackpot!

361
00:21:22,260 --> 00:21:25,600
Instead of raising my blood pressure,
raise our salaries, Chief!

362
00:21:27,940 --> 00:21:30,940
Ryo-chan has 20 cards, and the Chief has 19.

363
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:33,260
Only two cards are left.

364
00:21:33,260 --> 00:21:36,760
I won't lose to Ryotsu!

365
00:21:37,760 --> 00:21:40,920
Heh heh, I remember it!

366
00:21:40,920 --> 00:21:44,200
The toilet is upstairs in the study.

367
00:21:44,200 --> 00:21:47,420
Don't just eat your wife's
homemade lunch, Terai.

368
00:21:47,420 --> 00:21:48,100
The toilet!

369
00:21:48,300 --> 00:21:49,620
Damn it!

370
00:21:52,180 --> 00:21:53,140
Found it!

371
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:55,380
That's my win!

372
00:21:59,240 --> 00:22:00,760
That makes it even.

373
00:22:01,440 --> 00:22:03,140
You dirty cheat!

374
00:22:04,680 --> 00:22:07,260
Okay, here's the last card!

375
00:22:07,760 --> 00:22:09,820
I'm definitely going to turn this around.

376
00:22:09,820 --> 00:22:10,560
This year, you know,

377
00:22:11,180 --> 00:22:12,700
Cheating like that,
without even reading the card!

378
00:22:12,700 --> 00:22:14,080
This time, I've won for sure!

379
00:22:16,480 --> 00:22:16,880
What?

380
00:22:17,540 --> 00:22:18,480
It won't open!

381
00:22:20,720 --> 00:22:21,740
Don't be naive, Ryotsu.

382
00:22:21,740 --> 00:22:25,000
I locked that study just in case.

383
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:25,380
Damn it!

384
00:22:26,060 --> 00:22:27,960
After all, the one who laughs last is

385
00:22:30,800 --> 00:22:31,520
The key's gone.

386
00:22:31,520 --> 00:22:32,900
That's strange.

387
00:22:32,900 --> 00:22:36,340
So that means the Chief can't get in either.

388
00:22:37,760 --> 00:22:38,940
Fine, forget it!

389
00:22:40,140 --> 00:22:41,860
Those two are taking forever.

390
00:22:44,800 --> 00:22:46,480
They went outside, didn't they?

391
00:22:48,840 --> 00:22:49,800
Huh?

392
00:22:51,320 --> 00:22:52,360
Still not here.

393
00:22:53,820 --> 00:22:55,080
What's that noise?

394
00:22:58,440 --> 00:22:59,540
It's in here!

395
00:23:03,160 --> 00:23:04,700
What's going on?

396
00:23:07,760 --> 00:23:08,680
Whoa!

397
00:23:08,680 --> 00:23:10,860
Damn it!

398
00:23:14,620 --> 00:23:15,740
Whoa!

399
00:23:15,740 --> 00:23:16,120
Whoa!

400
00:23:16,120 --> 00:23:18,560
My card's location is...

401
00:23:18,560 --> 00:23:19,780
Chief

402
00:23:19,780 --> 00:23:21,200
You were a little slow, weren't you?

403
00:23:21,200 --> 00:23:23,060
I win.

404
00:23:23,060 --> 00:23:26,380
Well, Chief,
you did pretty well for your age.

405
00:23:26,380 --> 00:23:28,960
Well, at next year's New Year's party,

406
00:23:28,960 --> 00:23:32,000
Next year's New Year's party,

407
00:23:34,240 --> 00:23:35,360
absolutely

408
00:23:35,360 --> 00:23:38,880
Yeah! You're the one who's
not getting a single bite!

409
00:23:47,580 --> 00:23:51,200
Just as I expected, it's turned out
this way again this year, hasn't it.

410
00:23:56,140 --> 00:24:01,540
Watch again this year too! Kochira
Katsushika-ku Kameari Kōen-mae Hashutsujo!

411
00:24:05,360 --> 00:24:08,580
Dad's sick? It's probably just
lumbago or something, right?

412
00:24:08,780 --> 00:24:12,080
It's nothing serious. He'll get over
it if he sleeps for two or three days.

413
00:24:12,380 --> 00:24:14,125
Unfortunately,
I'm too overcome with emotion.

414
00:24:14,175 --> 00:24:16,740
I can't bring myself to cross
the threshold of my parents' home.

415
00:24:17,240 --> 00:24:21,000
Next time: Japan's most irresponsible parent and child.
See you then.

416
00:24:29,780 --> 00:24:32,660
Even if you stop the clock,

417
00:24:34,280 --> 00:24:37,760
time keeps passing.

418
00:24:39,360 --> 00:24:42,600
Make a sour face and cry,

419
00:24:44,380 --> 00:24:47,980
laugh it off and keep on living.

420
00:24:50,380 --> 00:24:53,020
Even if today

421
00:24:55,440 --> 00:24:57,920
is rainy,

422
00:25:24,940 --> 00:25:30,260
the sun is calling you
from outside the door.

